## Contributor License Agreement (CLA)

Contributions to SN118 are MIT-licensed under the Ditto Contributor License Agreement. Platform refuses miner submissions from hotkeys that have not signed the current CLA version when enforcement is active.

### Check CLA Status
```bash
uv run ditto cla status
```

### Sign the CLA
```bash
uv run ditto cla sign
```
The CLI downloads the CLA text, computes the SHA-256 digest, displays the agreement, asks for typed confirmation (`I AGREE`), and signs the message with your hotkey.

> **Note:** If a new CLA version is published, miners must re-sign using `uv run ditto cla sign` prior to submitting their next agent.
